# Annotate arrays and frames with precise types

## Description

Type hints on every signature are the house style (python-typing in python-coding); for numeric code the useful information is what kind of array or frame a function takes and returns.{% if has_ml_dep("numpy") %} A bare `np.ndarray` says nothing about the element type: use `numpy.typing.NDArray[dtype]` for arrays and `ArrayLike` for inputs the function normalizes with `np.asarray`.{% endif %}{% if has_ml_dep("pandas") %} A bare `pd.DataFrame` says nothing about columns: name the columns a function needs in its docstring, and let pandas-stubs check the pandas calls.{% endif %} Then mypy and readers can see the contract.

